Stop xterm.js from treating LF as CR+LF.

Freshell creates its terminals with convertEol: true, which real terminals
never do. Programs that put the tty in classic raw mode (-opost) emit a bare
LF followed by relative cursor moves (e.g. "\n\e[34D") and rely on LF keeping
the column. Antigravity CLI (agy) draws this way, so its logo, prompt and
completion list land too far left (danshapiro/freshell#790).

In cooked mode the kernel's ONLCR already turns LF into CR+LF, and Node's
raw mode keeps ONLCR on, so ordinary shells and Node-based CLIs are unaffected.

